version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/eduardogc8/QA-CompletenessRelevance"
repository-code: "https://github.com/eduardogc8/QA-CompletenessRelevance"
abstract: >-
  106 instruction-type questions in Computer Science, each with two long answers
  (one written by a Reddit user, one generated by GPT-4) scored 0-100 for
  completeness and 0-100 for relevance by four expert annotators, plus an
  expert-written reference answer per question. Intended for meta-evaluation:
  measuring how well an automatic evaluation metric agrees with human judgement.
keywords:
  - question answering
  - answer evaluation
  - completeness
  - relevance
  - long-form answers
  - non-factoid questions
  - meta-evaluation
  - evaluation metrics
